# hsm-sim 0.1.0: lifecycle
# Three files are written, age past migrate_after_s and are copied to tape
# (premigrated). Later writes push the cache over its high watermark, so the
# least recently used premigrated copies are purged to stubs. A read of a stub
# is a miss and triggers a recall; the second read is a hit.
# cache 1000 MB, watermarks 80% high / 50% low
# 1 drive(s), 3 tape(s) x 4000 MB, mount 60 s, seek 20 s, 100 MB/s
# scan every 300 s, migrate after 600 s, auto-repack off

== timeline ==
00:00:00  write     alpha.dat 200 MB (new) cache 200/1000 MB
00:00:30  write     beta.dat 200 MB (new) cache 400/1000 MB
00:01:00  write     gamma.dat 200 MB (new) cache 600/1000 MB
00:10:00  scan      1 file(s) at least 600 s old, migration queued
00:10:00  migrate   start on drive0: 1 file(s) 200 MB -> T01 (aged): alpha.dat, 82 s, done at 00:11:22
00:11:22  migrate   done -> T01: 1 file(s) premigrated [T01 200/4000 MB]
00:11:22  migrate   start on drive0: 2 file(s) 400 MB -> T01 (aged): beta.dat, gamma.dat, 24 s, done at 00:11:46
00:11:40  read      alpha.dat hit (premigrated)
00:11:46  migrate   done -> T01: 2 file(s) premigrated [T01 600/4000 MB]
00:20:00  write     delta.dat 300 MB (new) cache 900/1000 MB
00:20:00  purge     2 file(s) 400 MB for watermark cycle (down to 50%): beta.dat, gamma.dat -> stubs, cache 500/1000 MB
00:30:00  read      beta.dat miss: stub only, recall queued from T01
00:30:00  recall    start on drive0: 1 file(s) 200 MB from T01 in tape order: beta.dat, 22 s, done at 00:30:22
00:30:00  scan      1 file(s) at least 600 s old, migration queued
00:30:00  wait      migrate open tape T01 is in use
00:30:22  recall    done from T01: 1 file(s) back on disk cache 700/1000 MB
00:30:22  served    beta.dat: 1 read(s) served after waiting 22 s
00:30:22  migrate   start on drive0: 1 file(s) 300 MB -> T01 (aged): delta.dat, 23 s, done at 00:30:45
00:30:45  migrate   done -> T01: 1 file(s) premigrated [T01 900/4000 MB]
00:31:40  read      beta.dat hit (premigrated)
00:40:00  read      gamma.dat miss: stub only, recall queued from T01
00:40:00  recall    start on drive0: 1 file(s) 200 MB from T01 in tape order: gamma.dat, 22 s, done at 00:40:22
00:40:00  purge     2 file(s) 500 MB for watermark cycle (down to 50%): alpha.dat, delta.dat -> stubs, cache 400/1000 MB
00:40:22  recall    done from T01: 1 file(s) back on disk cache 400/1000 MB
00:40:22  served    gamma.dat: 1 read(s) served after waiting 22 s

